{
  "quest.427682661459BB4F.title": "&bStabilizing Your Enchantments",
  "task.1B78C40E21D23DD0.title": "Upgraded Hellshelves",
  "quest.0EE35D6E57FAD973.quest_subtitle": "Enchantment Storage!",
  "quest.34644FD6DAAE8F0C.quest_desc": [
    "Every hammer past the basic size needs a core. The first &dImpact Core&r uses up a Netherite Hammer, and each core after it is made from the one before.",
    "",
    "Impact hammers dig 3x3x3 instead of 3x3.",
  ],
  "task.1E99CDD9919D994A.title": "&aArtisan Scrolls",
  "quest.34644FD6DAAE8F0C.title": "&dThe Netherite Toll",
  "quest.6F16FFDCE6A35C31.title": "&bMining Gadgets",
  "quest.4BCEA2880B22CC55.title": "&6Artifacts",
  "quest.6F16FFDCE6A35C31.quest_desc": [
    "A &bMining Gadget&r is a powered laser drill you point at a wall.",
    "",
    "It comes in three tiers, &aMK1&r through &dMK3&r, and the real depth is in the &3Modification Table&r, where you fit upgrade modules:",
    "",
    "- &2Battery&r 1-3 for capacity, &aEfficiency&r 1-5 for power draw.",
    "- &a3x3&r and &aRange&r for how much you break at once.",
    "- &2Fortune&r and &aSilk Touch&r for what you get out of it.",
    "- &aVoid Junk&r throws away cobble and dirt as you mine.",
    "- &2Light Placer&r drops light behind you so nothing spawns in the tunnel.",
    "- &aFreeze&r handles lava and water you break into.",
  ],
  "quest.27E2F70FDEE0F003.title": "A Soul Bound Amulet",
  "quest.3D8CC5CFBD665D40.title": "&6Little Joys",
  "quest.4498E3F4B2DC24FC.quest_desc": [
    "To get started on getting your ultimate &eApotheosis&r gear, you'll need to fight monsters or explore the world for &bGems&r!",
    "",
    "&bGems&r are crystals that provide powerful bonuses when applied to &bAffix&r items.",
    "",
    "To apply a &bGem&r to an item, you must combine it with the item in a &2Smithing Table&r. The item must have an open &aGem Socket&r for this to work.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Gems give different bonuses when slotted in different item types, and can be upgraded in the &aGem Cutting Table&r.",
    "",
    "&cUnique Gems&r can only be socketed once per item, while most other gems can be socketed multiple times for stacking bonuses.",
    "",
    "There are a variety of &eApotheosis&r &bGems&r, which you can get by killing mobs and bosses.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "&bGems&r can also be crushed by an anvil to create &aGem Dust&r.",
    "",
    "You can use &aGem Dust&r for a variety of things, but the first thing you'll want to make is a &2Salvaging Table&r!",
  ],
  "task.601DC826C875D69F.title": "BEER Modifiers",
  "quest.17CD2138836B714A.quest_desc": [
    "Some chests are far better for artifacts than others.",
    "",
    "- &aBastion treasure rooms&r: 65% of chests hold one.",
    "- &2Big underwater ruins&r: 45%.",
    "- &aWoodland mansions&r: 40%.",
    "",
    "Brushing suspicious sand and gravel turns one up about 6% of the time.",
  ],
  "quest.23D4C14AE83B5C7A.quest_desc": [
    "A &cMimic&r looks exactly like a chest until you open it, and every one of them drops an artifact when it dies.",
    "",
    "They hide in underground campsites between y -60 and y 40, where about a third of the chests are mimics.",
  ],
  "task.77F4EF2435BBA602.title": "Reset Athletics",
  "quest.722901B4259D8AEC.quest_desc": [
    "The next goal is to push &aEterna&r to 60, with &cQuanta&r and &dArcana&r both at 40. You'll need to reach &5Ascent &bWorld Tier&r for this.",
    "",
    "This will require upgrading the &dInfused Bookshelves&r. ",
  ],
  "quest.4BDD9230BBA6C0A0.title": "The Unlimited Power of Hearts",
  "quest.4BCEA2880B22CC55.quest_desc": [
    "&eArtifacts&r are passive trinkets you find rather than craft, mostly out of &aMimics&r and chests in the world.",
    "",
    "They slot into your Curios and simply work. A few worth watching for:",
    "",
    "- &aCloud in a Bottle&r gives you a double jump.",
    "- &2Flippers&r and &aAqua-Dashers&r for moving in water.",
    "- &aFeral Claws&r and &2Digging Claws&r for attack and mining speed.",
    "- &2Crystal Heart&r for extra health.",
    "- &aCross Necklace&r for longer invulnerability.",
    "- &2Antidote Vessel&r clears bad effects.",
    "- &aEverlasting Beef&r and &2Eternal Steak&r never run out.",
    "",
    "&7&oThey stack with everything. Check any chest you open.&r",
  ],
  "quest.4DF8D485A9EDD069.quest_desc": [
    "Cows you kill yourself have a 0.2% chance to drop &6Everlasting Beef&r, food that is never used up.",
    "",
    "Cook it into &6Eternal Steak&r for a better meal that also never runs out.",
  ],
  "quest.172FD7459907AADE.title": "Reset Ranged",
  "task.7AFA5CC185A71520.title": "Welcome to &eApotheosis",
  "quest.3A7774F5F0FD174E.title": "Upgraded Shelves",
  "quest.3900E67C8B833980.title": "&aArtisan Scrolls",
  "quest.00249E1AFEF0051A.title": "A Better Movement",
  "quest.401680035DEE0D0A.quest_desc": [
    "Every gun in this mod feeds on the same &aBullet&r, so a single stack of ammo covers your whole collection.",
    "",
    "Craft them from &aBlackpowder&r and metal. &aIron&r returns 16 bullets per craft against only 4 from &2copper&r, so once you can spare the iron, stop using copper.",
    "",
    "&7&oKeep the crafting ingredients on you. Running dry mid-fight is the usual way these guns get you killed.&r",
  ],
  "quest.750007D8FAA2EA03.quest_desc": [
    "Two numbers grow while you play. &aLevel&r comes from your experience. Whenever you gain experience with your bonded spirit out and within 32 blocks, it gets half as much. &aBond&r comes from time, one point a second while it is out with you.",
    "",
    "Grinding at a mob farm slows its learning to a tenth. Move three chunks away and that resets.",
    "",
    "Feed it its taming item once every ten minutes for a bond boost. Bond 5 turns on the species' special ability, and bond 15 and 30 make timed abilities run twice and four times as often.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Use it with an empty hand to open its pack. The pack is yours, not the spirit's, so nothing is lost when it dies or rests, and more slots open as bond rises.",
    "",
    "At level 30 the bond screen offers &6Prestige&r. The spirit returns to level 1 with a star, up to five, and keeps its bond and gear. If it dies, the charm brings it back after five minutes, less at high bond.",
  ],
  "quest.26D7C5298D95C69A.quest_desc": [
    "When crafting &bJewelry&r, &aBanding Materials&r can be used by themselves to grant effects and/or stat increases.",
    "",
    "Their main use, however, is to multiply &aGem&r effects with their quality multiplier.",
    "",
    "While most vanilla gems will work, you can also search for &a#jewelry_band&r in JEI for a list.",
  ],
  "quest.7244D5DADCF0D7A2.quest_desc": [
    "The &bSeashelf of Aquatic Filtration&r can be loaded with up to six enchanted books, and will block those enchantments from showing up again.",
    "",
    "Works with &cCursed Enchants&r as well!",
  ],
  "quest.3A53BB7A6B708966.title": "&cHellshelf Infusion",
  "quest.26B74124E89189F7.quest_desc": [
    "The base shelf for the final tier of enchanting.",
    "",
    "Besides being locked behind &dInfused Dragon's Breath&r, Endshelves are relatively cheap.",
  ],
  "quest.4352595953CF7834.quest_desc": [
    "Two hats in the &eIron's Arms 'n Artifice&r tab do real work. The &aCowboy Hat&r instantly reloads your gun on a kill, with a cooldown between triggers, and the &2Tricorne&r makes the first shot from a full magazine hit harder.",
    "",
    "Both start from a &aleather helmet&r, so they cost almost nothing. They take your head slot, so you are trading helmet armor for the effect.",
    "",
    "&7&oTake the Cowboy Hat into crowds and the Tricorne when one big opening shot decides the fight.&r",
  ],
  "quest.4DE483256F9E1D4F.quest_desc": [
    "The &aSigil of Withdrawal&r will remove all socketed &bGems&r on an item without damaging your item.",
  ],
  "quest.375EB6B5189844BD.quest_desc": [
    "The &cMutant Zombie&r has 150 health and gets back up three times after going down. Keep it on fire when it falls, or light the body with flint and steel, and it stays down. It always drops the &aHulk Hammer&r.",
  ],
  "task.1074D584B5693F60.title": "Any Spirit Gear",
  "quest.1A7186E64604523F.title": "&eIron's Arms 'n Artifice",
  "quest.565F0889EF67521D.quest_desc": [
    "Seven spirits exist and each has its own way in. The &aMini Player&r is bought, not found. Every wandering trader sells one &aMini Player Spawn Egg&r for 32 emeralds, once per trader.",
    "",
    "Place it, then tame it with golden carrots at one in three per carrot. It wears your skin unless you type another player's name in the skin box on the bond screen, swings a copy of whatever weapon you are holding up close, and switches to a bow past six blocks.",
    "",
    "Its Helping Hand ability at bond 5 gives a 5% chance that stackable crafts come out doubled.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It is the slowest grower of the seven, so expect the long game. The others:",
    "- &aDirewolf&r: use a Golden Bone on any wolf.",
    "- &aT-Rex&r: dig a T-Rex Egg out of suspicious sand and let it hatch.",
    "- &aBaby Dragon&r: let lava flow against a placed dragon egg.",
    "- &aNightfox&r: use a block of sculk on a fox.",
    "- &aGremlin&r: feed a rabbit a carrot, then cooked chicken after midnight.",
    "- &aQuokka&r: found wild in jungles.",
  ],
  "quest.4352595953CF7834.title": "&dHats With Benefits",
  "quest.7313C557C45DCFAD.quest_desc": [
    "Refund your spent skill points in the Melee tree.",
  ],
  "quest.31A91FBA7673D2B3.quest_desc": [
    "Equip a full set of &2Uncommon&r affix gear or better and kill one &cApothic Invader&r.",
    "",
    "Invaders only spawn while Frontier or a higher tier is active, so switch tiers before you go hunting.",
  ],
  "quest.59CBFA5583139A3B.title": "{\"text\": \"Reforging Table\", \"color\": \"#B900B9\"}",
  "quest.79A0CEB28D8EC670.title": "&6Destruction",
  "quest.67E71C9B1037A2C0.title": "&cBone Armor",
  "task.46C4540DF9CFCF9E.title": "Reset Athletics",
  "quest.565F0889EF67521D.title": "&aA Player in Miniature",
  "quest.044A192E503B766B.title": "Patch Me Up!",
  "quest.718A5799ACCEFFF3.title": "&dTiered Spawner Runes",
  "quest.226E5BD0BEB1BA75.quest_desc": [
    "These are unique shelves that provide certain bonuses like adding 100% &cQuanta&r, or removing &cQuanta&r and &5Arcana&r.",
  ],
  "quest.2722C0E2E8993658.title": "&6Level 100 Enchanting",
  "quest.268CC540E5B605A9.title": "&dAchieving Enlightenment",
  "quest.18198810B4198724.title": "&aSpirit Gear",
  "quest.59CBFA5583139A3B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"The \", {\"text\": \"Reforging Table\", \"color\": \"#B900B9\"}, \" is an improved version of the \", {\"text\": \"Simple Reforging Table\", \"color\":\"#55FF55\"}, \", allowing you to reforge items of all rarities including \", {\"text\": \"Mythic\", \"color\":\"#EA6F14\"}, \" and \", {\"text\": \"Exalted\", \"color\":\"#FBD174\"}, \" items.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.54013FF4444B76EB.title": "The Baubliest of Heart Canisters",
  "quest.5382CB05500E49DE.quest_desc": [
    "Once you've maximized your &aEterna&r, you'll want to craft the &zEnchanting Table of the Raven&r.",
    "",
    "This enchantment table allows you to manually configure your &aEterna&r, &cQuanta&r, and &dArcana&r values without requiring any nearby bookshelves.",
  ],
  "quest.192EB03700278BE2.quest_desc": [
    "The &dRelic Apple&r is more than just an ordinary apple. ",
    "",
    "It gives you buffs when eaten and heals you instantly upon consumption.",
  ],
  "quest.26B74124E89189F7.title": "&dEndshelf",
  "quest.0CF882A83FB8931D.title": "&3The Six-Shooter",
  "quest.00A7C1FE54F86429.quest_desc": [
    "&eApotheosis&r overhauls the vanilla enchanting system with three new values, allowing for high-level enchants with upgradable progression. You will want to manage these values as you progress through upgrading your enchanting setup:",
    "",
    "[\"\", {\"text\": \"Eterna\", \"color\": \"green\"}, \": The power of the enchanting table, capped based on the tier of your bookshelves as well as your \", {\"text\": \"World Tier\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"id\": \"ftbquests:link\", \"payload\": {\"quest_id\": \"011DBD2652E49B97\", \"page\": 1}, \"action\": \"custom\"}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Go to World Tiers Quest\"}}, \". This stat determines the maximum level of enchants.\"]",
    "",
    "&cQuanta&r: The chaos inherent when enchanting at higher power. This determines the randomness of enchants.",
    "",
    "&dArcana&r: The overall quality and quantity of the enchantments. This determines the rarity of enchants, as well as how many enchants are applied per use.",
  ],
  "quest.31A91FBA7673D2B3.title": "&bAscent",
  "quest.2722C0E2E8993658.quest_desc": [
    "The centerpiece of a fully completed enchanting setup. ",
    "",
    "The &dDraconic Endshelf&r provides no additional stats, but will boost your &aEterna&r by 20, allowing you to hit a max of &6100&r.",
    "",
    "The &dPearlescent Endshelf&r is the best general-purpose bookshelf, providing significant amounts of both &cQuanta&r and &5Arcana&r.",
  ],
  "quest.65DAC5AA05C91055.quest_desc": [
    "The top tier. Equip a full set of &5Epic&r affix gear or better and kill the &dEnder Dragon&r.",
    "",
    "Mobs are at their strongest here, and so are the rewards.",
  ],
  "quest.5B8C8E2EC1DA1FF0.quest_desc": [
    "The &bParaglider&r turns any drop into a controlled descent. Hold it while falling and you glide instead of landing badly.",
    "",
    "Gliding costs &astamina&r. &2Stamina Vessels&r make your stamina wheel bigger, a fifth of a wheel each, up to 10 vessels. In this pack they are sold by &6The Black Market&r, a roaming merchant that sometimes turns up in place of the Wandering Merchant. Spirit Orbs and Heart Containers are turned off.",
    "",
    "On foot it wears out fast, about &c125 seconds&r of continuous gliding. Repair it with &aleather&r in an anvil.",
    "",
    "&7&oAn Elytra also counts as a paraglider in this pack, and can be held and used the same way.&r",
  ],
  "quest.7552BF792403EF44.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Hellshelf of Masterful Sight&r gives you 2 &3Enchanting Clues&r per shelf instead of 1.",
  ],
  "quest.01D2CEAF59872C33.title": "&aGem Case",
  "quest.183211CBBF56C4E1.title": "&dChemical X",
  "quest.0EE35D6E57FAD973.title": "&dEnchantment Library",
  "quest.5B8C8E2EC1DA1FF0.title": "&bThe Paraglider",
  "quest.0DA16C872BC27E21.title": "&cMutant Monsters",
  "quest.180F6058F80F1E1B.quest_desc": [
    "Hurt a &cMutant Creeper&r before it dies and it leaves a &aCreeper Minion Egg&r behind. Break the egg for a &aCreeper Shard&r. A charged egg always gives one, an uncharged egg only a third of the time.",
    "",
    "Left alone for 60 to 100 minutes, the egg hatches into a tame Creeper Minion instead.",
  ],
  "quest.4BBF090D430EC4A9.title": "&6Artifact Collector",
  "task.4544EA17F4CDD321.title": "Understanding Affix Items",
  "quest.26D7C5298D95C69A.title": "&aBanding Materials",
  "quest.6CB85481E967E81A.title": "&6Building Gadgets",
  "quest.3A53BB7A6B708966.quest_desc": [
    "Infused with magical energy, your bookshelves unlock more possibilities.",
  ],
  "quest.2F50137C675E49F9.title": "&aScannable",
  "quest.401680035DEE0D0A.title": "&aBullets",
  "quest.464AED8311A32476.title": "&fUnderstanding &aAffix &ritems",
  "quest.29513BD00064E27D.title": "Reset Mining",
  "quest.31AF46B183F805E3.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Clockwork Rifle&r sits at the top of the ladder. It wants &6netherite&r, a &aClockwork Components&r set, a &2hopper&r and a redstone repeater, so it comes well after your first trip to the Nether.",
    "",
    "The &aArquebus&r shares the Clockwork tier for far less material if you would rather make the parts go further.",
    "",
    "&7&oSpend your best modifiers here. A slot on this rifle is worth more than a slot on a Flintlock.&r",
  ],
  "quest.427682661459BB4F.quest_desc": [
    "&cQuanta&r adds randomness to your enchanting rolls, and at max chaos, you will end up with either +100% or -100% power.",
    "",
    "&bStabilization&r cancels out the negative effects, meaning you get all the upside, and none of the downside.",
  ],
  "quest.26118B733B805236.title": "&7Haven",
  "quest.2AFF075509A04B7E.quest_desc": [
    "Wear a full set of affix armor, &fCommon&f rarity or better, and hold an affix weapon.",
    "",
    "Unlocking a tier does not switch to it. Open the tier screen and activate &aFrontier&r yourself.",
    "",
    "From Frontier on, &cApothic Invaders&r start spawning in your world.",
  ],
  "task.1597C2CB4B03B2C2.title": "Any #artifacts:artifacts",
  "quest.30689B890F5E7A03.quest_desc": [
    "To push your &6Eterna&r even higher, you will need to create and infuse &3Deepshelves&r and also reach the Summit &bWorld Tier&r.",
    "",
    "These shelves can push your &6Eterna&r to a max of &a75&r. ",
    "",
    "You can also use a &zDeepshelf of Arcane Treasures&r to allow your enchanting table to enchant &zTreasure Enchantments&r.",
  ],
  "task.0F868488088CDEC1.title": "BEER",
  "quest.011DBD2652E49B97.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\", {\"text\": \"Apotheosis\", \"color\": \"yellow\"}, \" has a \", {\"text\": \"World Tier\", \"color\": \"aqua\"}, \" system that can be accessed by pressing \", {\"keybind\": \"key.apotheosis.open_world_tier_select\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: CTRL + T\"}}, \".\"]",
    "",
    "[\"You start at \", {\"text\": \"Haven\", \"color\": \"#7E7E7E\"}, \" upon acquiring your first \", {\"text\": \"Affix Item\", \"color\": \"#55FF55\"}, \", and unlock more tiers as you advance in the mod.\"]",
    "",
    "Higher tiers increase mob stats and rewards across all dimensions, and reduce your max &aEterna&r cap. These can be viewed in the Tiers menu.",
  ],
  "quest.23C3A724DE53F3B2.title": "Reset Magic",
  "quest.24730AF0C707CF79.quest_desc": [
    "&cThis one is specific to this pack and you will not find it documented anywhere else.",
    "",
    "Equip a &bParaglider&r onto a &ahorse&r and it becomes a &dpegasus&r. The horse gains flight, and you fly it like you would ride it.",
    "",
    "Anything that counts as a paraglider works, including an &aElytra&r, though an elytra's lower durability only keeps a horse up for about 11 minutes.",
    "",
    "Flight drains a paraglider far more slowly than gliding on foot does. Expect roughly &a62 minutes&r of airtime from a full one against about two minutes on your own legs. Repair it with &aleather&r in an anvil, same as ever.",
    "",
    "&7&oIf the wings equip but the horse never leaves the ground, the paraglider has no durability left.&r",
  ],
  "quest.38E0212362E87E99.title": "&dEndersoul Hand",
  "quest.4BBF090D430EC4A9.quest_desc": [
    "Carry ten artifacts at once. Any ten count, repeats included.",
    "",
    "Mimics and the treasure chests above are the fastest way to get there.",
  ],
  "quest.7E88C7654F281E43.quest_desc": [
    "[\"The \", {\"text\": \"Augmenting Table\", \"color\": \"#EA6F14\"}, \" is an end-game crafting station used to augment the individual \", {\"text\": \"Affixes\", \"color\": \"#55FFFF\"}, \" of an item.\"]",
    "",
    "It has two different uses:",
    "",
    "[\"Firstly, it can upgrade an existing \", {\"text\": \"Affix\", \"color\": \"#55FFFF\"}, \", costing two \", {\"text\": \"Sigils of Enhancement\", \"color\": \"#EA6F14\"}, \" to upgrade the \", {\"text\": \"Affix\", \"color\": \"#55FFFF\"}, \" by 25%. How much of a boost this provides varies per \", {\"text\": \"Affix\", \"color\": \"#55FFFF\"}, \".\"]",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "[\"Secondly, it can reroll an \", {\"text\": \"Affix\", \"color\": \"#55FFFF\"}, \", costing one \", {\"text\": \"Sigil of Enhancement\", \"color\": \"#EA6F14\"}, \" to swap out a selected \", {\"text\": \"Affix\", \"color\": \"#55FFFF\"}, \" for another of the same type. The alternative options will be shown on the left.\"]",
    "",
    "[\"The \", {\"text\": \"Augmenting Table\", \"color\": \"#EA6F14\"}, \" has two input slots. The upper slot holds the item you wish to \", {\"text\": \"Augment\", \"color\": \"#FF55FF\"}, \", which must be an \", {\"text\": \"Affix\", \"color\": \"#55FFFF\"}, \" item. The lower slot holds the \", {\"text\": \"Sigils of Enhancement\", \"color\": \"#EA6F14\"}, \" used for \", {\"text\": \"Augmenting\", \"color\": \"#FF55FF\"}, \".\"]",
  ],
  "quest.27E2F70FDEE0F003.quest_desc": [
    "Going further, the &bSoul Amulet&r holds even more canisters. Each &aSoul Canister&r you add raises your max health further.",
    "",
    "It also works like a &6Totem of Undying&r. If you would &cdie&r, a &aSoul Canister&r is consumed and reverts back to a &bBlue Heart Canister&r instead.",
  ],
  "quest.01D2CEAF59872C33.quest_desc": [
    "The &dGem Case&r is used to store and upgrade &bGems&r. ",
    "",
    "It's a direct upgrade to the &aGem Cutting Table&r, which is only used to upgrade gems.",
    "",
    "Upgrading a &bGem&r costs &aGem Dust&r, rarity materials, and a second &bGem&r of the same rarity. The material and dust cost of upgrading a &bGem&r increases with its rarity. The exact upgrade costs will be shown in the interface.",
  ],
  "quest.44C341DE3BCD64CC.quest_desc": [
    "This upgraded version of the &dEnchantment Library&r can store enchantments values up to level 31.",
    "",
    "Please note that the actual enchanted books are still capped at normal pack limits.",
  ],
  "quest.7244D5DADCF0D7A2.title": "&bFiltering Unwanted Enchants",
  "quest.3EFAC6FC58219F86.title": "&6Construction Sticks",
  "quest.266D0151DF0A7BA5.quest_desc": [
    "The &zVigor Bow&r works similar to a &bHeart Amulet&r. It has its own slots for &2canisters&r.",
    "",
    "Each &2canister&r adds &b1&r additional damage and Draw Speed to the Bow.",
  ],
  "quest.496903AB7E8A0A92.title": "&fWelcome to &eIron's Gems \\&\\ Jewelry&r!",
  "quest.75BC832C835585E2.title": "&3Machined Parts",
  "quest.78BCE2A8F87EB08B.title": "&zThe Sword of Friendship",
  "quest.4BCA8A5C3F80D375.quest_desc": [
    "The &aSigil of Unnaming&r removes the Affix name of an item, reverting it to its normal item name.",
    "",
    "For example: &dEndawn the Ogre Slayer's Windswept Burnt Shoes of the Spellwarden&r will be renamed to &dBurnt Shoes&r.",
  ],
  "quest.0CF882A83FB8931D.quest_desc": [
    "The &aSix-Shooter&r is the first gun on the middle parts tier. It takes a &2Mechanical Components&r set, a &ahopper&r, iron and a log.",
    "",
    "The &aBlackpowder Revolver&r sits on the same tier, with &2Blackpowder&r in place of one of the iron ingots. Compare both tooltips in JEI and take whichever fire rate and reload suit how you play.",
  ],
  "quest.3D8CC5CFBD665D40.quest_desc": [
    "&eLittle Joys&r adds small surprises that show up on their own while you play. There is nothing to craft and nothing to build; you just have to notice them.",
    "",
    "&aDig Spots&r appear in the ground near you as you move around. Dig one up for a bit of treasure.",
    "",
    "&bFishing Spots&r are patches of bubbles on the water. Cast into one and you pull out treasure instead of a fish. If that sounds familiar, it is almost exactly how &3Nautec's&r &blucky zones&r work, and the two are separate systems that both reward paying attention to the water.",
    "",
    "&6Gold Rushes&r and &aDrop Rushes&r trigger while you are mining and breaking blocks, scattering extra drops for you to collect.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "&3Fallen Stars&r streak down now and then. Catch one and it grants a blessing:",
    "",
    "- &aStar of Abundance&r duplicates block drops.",
    "- &2Star of Prosperity&r bonemeals what you plant and gives breeding animals twins.",
    "- &aStar of Fate&r and &2Star of Serenity&r round out the set.",
    "",
    "Each blessing has a strength that fades as you use it, from &7Fading&r up through &fGlowing&f and &3Radiant&r to &6Brilliant&r.",
    "",
    "&7&oNothing here needs to be chased. It is all bonus on top of whatever you were already doing.&r",
  ],
  "quest.60FDF616DEDE5E73.title": "&bApothic Gems&r!",
  "task.7730E1475241BC5B.title": "Reset Athletics",
  "quest.67E71C9B1037A2C0.quest_desc": [
    "A &cMutant Skeleton&r shatters into 18 bone pieces when it dies. Right-click each piece to pick it up before it disappears after 6,000 ticks. One skeleton gives exactly one armor set.",
    "",
    "The skull helmet adds a level of Multishot to any bow you fire while wearing it.",
  ],
  "quest.4DF8D485A9EDD069.title": "&6Eternal Steak",
  "quest.23C3A724DE53F3B2.quest_desc": [
    "Refund your spent skill points in the Magic tree.",
  ],
  "quest.180F6058F80F1E1B.title": "&cCreeper Shard",
  "quest.0DA16C872BC27E21.quest_desc": [
    "Now and then a zombie, skeleton, creeper or enderman spawns as a &cmutant&r, a much bigger version with its own attacks and a signature drop. Mutants appear wherever the normal mob does, at 5% of its spawn weight.",
  ],
  "quest.54013FF4444B76EB.quest_desc": [
    "The &2Heart Canister&r is the most important part of the mod. &2Canisters&r are slotted in &aAmulets&r and used to increase your max health points.",
    "",
    "Each &2Canister&r adds a single new heart and stacks at &b10&r. ",
  ],
  "quest.37F99696A47264FD.quest_desc": [
    "This chapter is all about teaching you some of the different ways to craft, enhance, and enchant any gear you might need on your adventures!",
  ],
  "quest.17CD2138836B714A.title": "&6Treasure Hunting",
  "quest.315810E48F0849F5.quest_desc": [
    "&bPower Armor&r is a powered four-piece set that you build up rather than enchant.",
    "",
    "The &aCompressor&r presses ingots into plates, but it does not make &2Copper Wire&r. In this pack the wire comes from an Energized Power &aCutter&r, a hand tool, used on Copper Plates. Then take the finished pieces to the &aArmor Modification Table&r and start fitting modules.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "What you can slot in:",
    "- &aEnergy&r and &2Solar&r keep the suit charged.",
    "- &2Jetpack&r gets you off the ground.",
    "- &aSpeed&r moves you faster.",
    "- &2Plating&r soaks more damage.",
    "- &aNight Vision&r lights up the dark.",
    "- &2Laser&r gives the suit a weapon.",
    "",
    "A Battery in the suit is what everything else runs on. Fit Solar early and you'll rarely have to think about charging it again.",
  ],
  "quest.03DB41A64E74FF33.title": "&bGun Modifiers",
  "quest.7E685EAD7FB60B45.quest_desc": [
    "The &aSalvaging Table&r is used to break down affix items into their corresponding rarity materials:",
    "",
    "&#7E7E7ECommon - Mysterious Scrap Metal",
    "&#55FF55Uncommon - Timeworn Fabric",
    "&#5454FCRare - Luminous Crystal Shard",
    "&#B900B9Epic - Arcane Sands",
    "&#EA6F14Mythic - Godforged Pearls",
    "&#FBD174Exalted - Aurichalcum Relics",
    "",
    "The &aSalvaging Table&r can be automated by sending items in from the top or sides, and extracting them from the bottom of the table. Don't lose any items!",
  ],
  "quest.3208AF90091D1B6B.quest_desc": [
    "Using the &aSimple Reforging Table&r, you can now reforge an item with brand new affixes.",
    "",
    "Reforging is not limited to items that already have &bAffixes&r, and can be performed with any valid item, any number of times.",
    "",
    "The &aSimple Reforging Table&r allows you to reforge items up to &9Rare&r rarity. You'll need to upgrade this table if you wish to reforge higher rarity items.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Reforging Tables have three input slots:",
    "",
    "The center slot holds the item you wish to reforge, the top-left slot holds the rarity materials for the rarity you would like to reforge with, and the bottom-right slot holds &aSigils of Rebirth&r, which are used as fuel during reforging.",
    "",
    "There is a base cost of experience, sigils, and materials for reforges of each rarity, which can be doubled or tripled if choosing the other two options.",
  ],
  "quest.78BCE2A8F87EB08B.quest_desc": [
    "The &zVitality Blade&r works similar to a &bHeart Amulet&r. It has its own slots for &2canisters&r.",
    "",
    "Each &2canister&r adds &e1&r additional damage to the sword.",
  ],
  "quest.1A7186E64604523F.quest_desc": [
    "&eIron's Arms 'n Artifice&r arms you with black-powder firearms, from a crude &aFlintlock&r up to a &6Clockwork Rifle&r, and lets you rebuild each one with modifiers that change how it shoots.",
    "",
    "It all starts with &aBlackpowder&r. Two per craft from charcoal and redstone, and there is a second recipe that folds in spare &agunpowder&r if you have it.",
    "",
    "&7&oGuns need ammo and a manual reload. Set your reload keybind before you carry one into a fight.&r",
  ],
  "quest.3EFAC6FC58219F86.quest_desc": [
    "A &aConstruction Stick&r places a whole row or face of blocks in one click, pulling from your inventory.",
    "",
    "They come in &aStickiest&r, &2Copper&r, Iron, Diamond and Netherite, each reaching further than the last.",
    "",
    "&aTemplates&r change what a stick does: &2Destruction&r removes instead of places, Replacement swaps one block for another, Angel builds into thin air, and Unbreakable and Battery keep it running.",
  ],
  "quest.226E5BD0BEB1BA75.title": "&aMiscellaneous Shelves",
  "quest.44C341DE3BCD64CC.title": "&dLibrary of Alexandria",
  "quest.172FD7459907AADE.quest_desc": [
    "Refund your spent skill points in the Ranged tree.",
  ],
  "quest.03DB41A64E74FF33.quest_desc": [
    "Every gun carries &bmodifier slots&r. Modifiers are crafted items you slot into the weapon to change how it behaves, and you open the slot screen with the &bOpen Gun Modifiers&r keybind while holding the gun.",
    "",
    "They cover most of what a firearm can do: &aScattershot&r for more bullets per pull, &2Steel Core&r and Lead Core for damage, Incendiary Tip for burn, Frozen Jacket for shrapnel, Voltaic Core for lightning chains, Seeking Powder for tracking, and Antigravity Powder to flatten bullet drop.",
    "",
    "&cIllificers&r carry a randomized loadout of these and drop &aBlackpowder&r and &2emeralds&r. They count as illagers, so they arrive with raids and patrols.",
    "",
    "&7&oRead the tooltip before you commit a slot. Several modifiers pay for their effect by taking a stat away.&r",
  ],
  "task.247B79A552BA6CCE.title": "Gearing Up For Adventure!",
  "quest.52FD0AD73FBCBE3D.title": "&aHats",
  "quest.24730AF0C707CF79.title": "&dPegasus",
  "quest.398AF8F202DDD6AB.title": "&eJust Hammers",
  "quest.38E0212362E87E99.quest_desc": [
    "A dying &cMutant Enderman&r releases Endersoul Fragments. Right-click them to claim them before they explode, then drop an Eye of Ender within 8 blocks to get the &dEndersoul Hand&r.",
    "",
    "It teleports you up to 256 blocks. It has 240 durability, and each fragment you feed it repairs 60.",
  ],
  "quest.398AF8F202DDD6AB.quest_desc": [
    "&eJust Hammers&r mines a 3x3 area with every swing. The larger hammers reach further, up to the 5x5x5 Destructor.",
    "",
    "A hammer stops working at 0 durability instead of breaking, so repair it before it runs dry. Each repair item restores a third of its durability, and netherite restores all of it.",
  ],
  "quest.2F50137C675E49F9.quest_desc": [
    "The &aScanner&r pings the world around you and draws what it finds straight through the rock.",
    "",
    "On its own it does nothing. It takes &amodules&r, and each one teaches it to look for something different: &2Common Ores&r, Rare Ores, Fluids, Chests, Lootr containers, Spawners, Monsters, Animals or a specific Block you show it.",
    "",
    "&aRange Modules&r widen the sweep.",
  ],
  "quest.26118B733B805236.quest_desc": [
    "Every world starts in &7Haven&r. It unlocks the moment you pick up your first &aaffix item&r.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"The first time you open the tier screen with \", {\"keybind\": \"key.apotheosis.open_world_tier_select\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: CTRL + T\"}}, \" and close it, Haven is switched on for you.\"]",
    "",
    "Each tier above it has its own unlock requirements.",
  ],
  "quest.3AA445DE64D8E77D.quest_desc": [
    "Refund your spent skill points in the Athletics tree.",
  ],
  "task.574369B60421C9FF.title": "&aBanding Materials",
  "quest.722901B4259D8AEC.title": "Upgraded Shelves",
  "quest.4DE483256F9E1D4F.title": "&aSigil of Withdrawal",
  "task.2A88734461D7A62C.title": "Reset Athletics",
  "quest.31AF46B183F805E3.title": "&6The Clockwork Rifle",
  "quest.266D0151DF0A7BA5.title": "&zColorful Bullseye",
  "quest.52FD0AD73FBCBE3D.quest_desc": [
    "Some creatures spawn wearing hats. Kill one and that hat is added to your collection for good, ready to wear from the Hats menu.",
    "",
    "The menu key starts unbound in this pack. Set it under Hats in Controls.",
  ],
  "quest.3A7774F5F0FD174E.quest_desc": [
    "To get to the next upgrade, you want to get your &aEterna&r to &a45&r by reaching the &2Frontier &bWorld Tier&r. This can be done with upgraded shelves.",
    "",
    "The &cHellshelf&r is easier to craft, and focuses on boosting &cQuanta&r.",
    "",
    "&bSeashelves&r will require some fishing to get started, but builds up your &dArcana&r values instead.",
  ],
  "quest.3B4B61D505899B51.title": "&dWaystones",
  "quest.4498E3F4B2DC24FC.title": "&aGems",
  "quest.7552BF792403EF44.title": "&6Hellshelf of Masterful Sight",
  "quest.750007D8FAA2EA03.title": "&6Bond and Stars",
  "quest.5A6151C5CBCBAAF4.quest_desc": [
    "A &dHeart Amulet&r holds all your &2Heart Canisters&r. ",
    "",
    "You add them into the amulet and equip them in the &eCurios Slot&r.",
    "",
    "You can press Shift when hovering over the item to see how many Total Canisters is stored inside.",
    "",
    "You can have a total of &b40&r extra hearts in a base amulet.",
  ],
  "task.6B866D3A40E6B79C.title": "Reset Athletics",
  "quest.183211CBBF56C4E1.quest_desc": [
    "&dChemical X&r turns a normal creeper, enderman, skeleton, snow golem or zombie into its mutant form, so you can farm the drops instead of waiting for one to spawn.",
    "",
    "Pigs work too if you feed them a fermented spider eye first.",
  ],
  "quest.5A6151C5CBCBAAF4.title": "The Amulet of the Heart",
  "task.74E6C34609E1C526.title": "Salvaged Materials",
  "quest.79A0CEB28D8EC670.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Destruction Core&r is the end of the line. Its hammer clears a 5x5x5 cube, 125 blocks per swing.",
  ],
  "quest.192EB03700278BE2.title": "Fancy Apple",
  "quest.011DBD2652E49B97.title": "&fApothic World Tiers",
  "task.1DDB96A415840B51.title": "Artifacts",
  "task.2C718A1A0353A93C.title": "Upgraded Seashelves",
  "quest.00249E1AFEF0051A.quest_desc": [
    "The &bHeart Pulse Belt&r is a curio. While equipped, it grants increased movement speed, step assist, and increased jump height.",
    "",
    "Upgrade values can be seen on the next page.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "&cRed Heartpulse Belt&r: 1.5 Block Height Jump and slight speed increase.",
    "",
    "&6Yellow Heartpulse Belt&r: 2 Block Height Jump and moderate speed increase.",
    "",
    "&9Blue Heartpulse Belt&r: 2.5 Block Height Jump and fast speed increase.",
    "",
    "&aGreen Heartpulse Belt&r: 3 Block Height Jump and very fast speed increase.",
  ],
  "quest.1709DBEFF27D834B.title": "&dSummit",
  "task.1C0FFC5D4A1D00C7.title": "Extraction Tomes",
  "quest.496903AB7E8A0A92.quest_desc": [
    "&eIron's Gems \\&\\ Jewelry&r is a mod that focuses on combining materials and &bJewels&r to provide the player with special effects or stat increases.",
    "",
    "You will need to craft a &aJewelcrafting Station&r to begin making some basic &bJewelry&r items, but you'll need to purchase more advanced blueprints from the &zShop&r.",
    "",
    "[\"For a full list of compatible items, check out the \", {\"text\": \"Jewelry GuideMe\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,irons_jewelry:guide,irons_jewelry:index.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open Iron's Jewelry GuideMe\"}, \"underlined\": true}, \".\"]",
  ],
  "quest.4BDD9230BBA6C0A0.quest_desc": [
    "&aHearts&r are a key component of &eBaubley Heart Canisters&r.",
    "",
    "- &cRed Hearts&r: Drop from Apothic Mobs",
    "- &6Yellow Hearts&r: Drop from Bosses",
    "- &2Green Hearts&r: Drop from the Ender Dragon",
    "- &bBlue Hearts&r: Made from Crafting",
    "",
    "Hearts can also be eaten and will restore health based on the level.",
    "",
    "- &cRed&r: 10 Hearts per use.",
    "- &6Yellow&r: 20 Hearts per use.",
    "- &aGreen&r: 30 Hearts per use.",
    "- &bBlue&r: 40 Hearts per use.",
  ],
  "quest.3B4B61D505899B51.quest_desc": [
    "&dWaystones&r are the pack's answer to walking the same route twice.",
    "",
    "Place and name a &aWaystone&r and you can warp back to it from any other. A &2Sharestone&r links to every other Sharestone of the same color, no matter who placed it. A &aPortstone&r only works one way. You can warp out from it, but it never shows up as a destination.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "For traveling without a stone at the far end there are scrolls. A &aWarp Scroll&r is single use and a &2Bound Scroll&r remembers one destination. A &aReturn Scroll&r takes you to the nearest waystone you have activated.",
    "",
    "The &aWarp Stone&r is the reusable version. Each warp costs it 80 of its 10,000 durability on top of the experience cost, so it lasts about 125 trips.",
    "",
    "&7&oWaystones you find in villages are free to attune. Look for them before you start crafting your own.&r",
  ],
  "quest.2E7EBD2A61897192.title": "&fHotswapping Enchantments",
  "quest.6EE1C1B7FFB86C6C.title": "&aSigil of Socketing",
  "task.13E1E8B471826659.title": "Runes",
  "quest.4A0A19E73680034F.title": "Bookshelf Extended Enchantment Reach",
  "quest.469DBE287993C779.title": "&aThe Flintlock",
  "quest.2F2DC018DD6A2A23.title": "&aGems",
  "task.6B8F6B75C6182427.title": "Upgraded Deepshelves",
  "quest.469DBE287993C779.quest_desc": [
    "The &aFlintlock&r is the first gun you can build and the only one that needs no machined parts, just iron, a log, blackpowder and a flint and steel.",
    "",
    "Hover any gun to read its damage, reload time, ammo capacity and modifier slots. Guns that hold more than one shot also list a fire rate, and single-shot guns like this one list bullet speed instead.",
  ],
  "quest.00A7C1FE54F86429.title": "&6The Secrets of Enchanting",
  "quest.4BCA8A5C3F80D375.title": "&aSigil of Unnaming",
  "quest.4A0A19E73680034F.quest_desc": [
    "&e&lBEER&r&f (Bookshelf Extended Enchanting Reach) allows you to modify the range that enchanting tables scan for bookshelves:",
    "",
    "Normally, enchanting tables only look for bookshelves in a 5x5x3 area around them. With &e&lBEER&r, you can:",
    "",
    "• Expand the X and Z width (horizontal range)",
    "• Increase the Y height (vertical range)",
    "• Use special items to modify these dimensions",
    "• Create custom enchanting setups beyond vanilla limits",
    "",
    "",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "&l&aHow to Use &e&lBEER&r",
    "",
    "To modify an enchanting table's range:",
    "1. Hold the modifier item in your main hand",
    "2. Optionally hold a specific item in your offhand (to decrease range)",
    "3. Sneak (Shift) + Right-click on an enchanting table",
  ],
  "quest.7E685EAD7FB60B45.title": "&fThe &aSalvaging Table",
  "task.4B67D8495CB6403D.title": "&aGems",
  "quest.37F99696A47264FD.title": "&fGearing Up For Adventure!",
  "quest.464AED8311A32476.quest_desc": [
    "Before we dive into &eApotheosis&r, we need to cover what an &bAffix&r is!",
    "",
    "An &bAffix&r is the driving force behind all &eApotheosis&r gear. Each &bAffix&r is very similar to an enchantment, providing a bonus to the item it is attached to.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "&bAffix&r items can be found when exploring the world and their effects vary based on the item's rarity. They are more commonly dropped from &eApotheosis&r boss monsters which can be found in underground caves or have a chance to randomly appear during the night.",
    "",
    "There are a few different types of &bAffixes&r, each affecting a specific part of the item such as: Stats, Effects, Durability, and &bGem Sockets&r, which will be covered in the &bGems&r section.",
  ],
  "quest.2E7EBD2A61897192.quest_desc": [
    "Got a lot of random enchanted gear? Using a &dTome of Scrapping&r, you can break it down and extract some of the enchantments from it.",
    "",
    "The &dTome of Extraction&r will also remove all enchants, but will keep the item from being destroyed, allowing you to remove and replace any number of enchantments on an item at will.",
    "",
    "If you're looking for a specific enchantment for a specific tool, you can use &dTomes&r which can be crafted to only support a certain class of enchantments.",
  ],
  "quest.60FDF616DEDE5E73.quest_desc": [
    "&eApotheosis&r overhauls exploration and combat by creating a more RPG-like experience.",
    "",
    "Items and mobs you can find in the world can have special &bAffixes&r on them, making them much stronger, and sometimes giving them special abilities to make things even more fun!",
    "",
    "If you feel lost, you can always refer to the &aChronicle of Shadows&r, which is the guide book for the mod.",
  ],
  "quest.3208AF90091D1B6B.title": "&aSimple Reforging Table",
  "quest.044A192E503B766B.quest_desc": [
    "The &aHeart Patch&r works like a bandage. Using one heals you based on its tier. It has a cooldown, so be careful about relying on it as a lifeline.",
    "",
    "Each Tier Increases the base value healed.",
    "",
    "&cRed&r: 1 Heart per use.",
    "",
    "&6Yellow&r: 3 Hearts per use.",
    "",
    "&9Blue&r: 6 Hearts per use.",
    "",
    "&aGreen&r: 10 Hearts per use.",
  ],
  "quest.268CC540E5B605A9.quest_desc": [
    "Your final tier of bookshelves is locked behind the infusion of &dDragon's Breath&r.",
    "",
    "To do this, you will need 80 &aEterna&r, between 15 to 30 &cQuanta&r, and at least 60 &dArcana&r. ",
    "",
    "If you don't have enough &dArcana,&r you can use candles, which provide a small boost.",
  ],
  "quest.6EE1C1B7FFB86C6C.quest_desc": [
    "&aSigils of Socketing&r are used to increase the amount of &bGem Sockets&r of an &bAffix&r item.",
  ],
  "quest.5382CB05500E49DE.title": "&zEnchanting Table of the Raven",
  "quest.30689B890F5E7A03.title": "&3Venturing Deeper",
  "quest.1709DBEFF27D834B.quest_desc": [
    "Equip a full set of &9Rare&r affix gear or better and kill the &5Wither&r.",
    "",
    "You can drop back to any tier you have unlocked from the same screen if the mobs get ahead of your gear.",
  ],
  "quest.75BC832C835585E2.quest_desc": [
    "Better guns need better internals, and they come in three tiers that stack into each other.",
    "",
    "- &aSimple Mechanical Components&r: builds the Blunderbuss and Musket.",
    "- &2Mechanical Components&r: builds the Six-Shooter and Blackpowder Revolver.",
    "- &aClockwork Components&r: builds the Arquebus and Clockwork Rifle.",
    "",
    "Each tier consumes the one below it, so batch a few spare Simple sets before you start climbing.",
  ],
  "quest.6CB85481E967E81A.quest_desc": [
    "Where sticks handle rows, &eBuilding Gadgets&r handle shapes and whole structures.",
    "",
    "- &aBuilding Gadget&r places in configurable patterns.",
    "- &aExchanging Gadget&r swaps existing blocks for something else in place.",
    "- &aDestruction Gadget&r clears a volume in one go.",
    "- &aCopy Paste&r and &2Cut Paste&r Gadgets capture a build and stamp it down elsewhere.",
    "",
    "The &aTemplate Manager&r stores those captures as &2Templates&r and Redprints, so a design you got right once can be rebuilt anywhere.",
  ],
  "quest.65DAC5AA05C91055.title": "&6Pinnacle",
  "quest.7E88C7654F281E43.title": "{\"text\":\"Augmenting Items\", \"color\":\"#EA6F14\"}",
  "quest.7313C557C45DCFAD.title": "Reset Melee",
  "quest.718A5799ACCEFFF3.quest_desc": [
    "Four runes, one named for each tier past Haven, push an &aApothic Spawner&r well beyond the basic upgrades. Use a rune on a spawner to apply it.",
    "",
    "The first three each need a salvage material from gear one rarity higher than the last, so they arrive in step with your tiers. The &aThundering&r rune is made in the &6FTB Fabricator&r once you have defeated the Ender Dragon.",
    "",
    "- &aFrontiersman's&r: 7 mobs every 7.5 to 30 seconds.",
    "- &2Wayfarer's&r: 10 mobs every 5 to 20 seconds.",
    "- &aMountaineer's&r: 13 mobs every 2.5 to 10 seconds.",
    "- &2Thundering&r: 16 mobs every second.",
    "",
    "A rune sets those values outright instead of adding to them, so using a lower rune on a spawner you already upgraded makes it worse.",
  ],
  "quest.315810E48F0849F5.title": "&bPower Armor",
  "quest.2AFF075509A04B7E.title": "&aFrontier",
  "quest.3900E67C8B833980.quest_desc": [
    "&aArtisan Scrolls&r can be found as loot or bought from &zShops&r.",
    "",
    "To learn a &bJewel&r blueprint simply right-click with an &aArtisan Scroll&r in hand.",
    "",
    "There are 2 special &aArtisan Scrolls&r that will teach you how to craft &6Duality&r jewelry.",
    "",
    "This jewelry takes both the attributes from the &bMetal&r and the &dGem&r, and has a higher quality overall.",
  ],
  "quest.18198810B4198724.quest_desc": [
    "Every spirit has one gear slot and each species has its own gear. Use the item on your tamed spirit to equip it, and it hands back whatever it was wearing. The bond screen has a button to take gear off.",
    "",
    "Gear stays on through rest and revive. Releasing the bond drops it at the spirit's feet.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "- &aBoxing Gloves&r: T-Rex. Reaches three blocks further and hits for two more.",
    "- &2Dragon Tablet&r: Baby Dragon. Its breath becomes a meteor.",
    "- &aRunning Shoes&r: Nightfox. 60% faster, and Swift Step gives you Speed II.",
    "- &2Battery&r: Gremlin. Speeds up nearby machines and shocks hostiles next to it.",
    "- &aQuokka Snack&r: Quokka. A chance to charm nearby monsters into fighting each other.",
    "- &2Chestplates&r and &aWolf Armor&r: Mini Player and Direwolf. Any chestplate or any wolf armor, and neither ever loses durability.",
  ],
  "quest.2F2DC018DD6A2A23.quest_desc": [
    "&aGems&r are the part of most &bJewelry&r that grants effects or attributes.",
    "",
    "Different pieces of &bJewelry&r are affected by &aGems&r in different ways, so be sure to check each piece carefully before crafting.",
    "",
    "While most vanilla gems will work, you can also search for &a#jewelry_gem&r in JEI for a list.",
  ],
  "quest.29513BD00064E27D.quest_desc": [
    "Refund your spent skill points in the Mining tree.",
  ],
  "quest.0EE35D6E57FAD973.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Enchantment Library&r acts as a storage for enchantments. With enough low level enchants, it can also create books of higher level enchants for you.",
  ],
  "quest.23D4C14AE83B5C7A.title": "&6Mimics",
}